This file records details of all data files in the data_cache folder of the R project biodiversity-wind-solar.

These files are not included in the repository because of their size (several are >1 GB) and because they are freely available from their original sources, listed below. They are only needed to re-run scripts/spatial_dataprep.R (which builds data_output/windsolar_environments.csv and data_output/footprint_classes.csv), the climate density plots in scripts/spatial_figures.R, the biome comparison in scripts/sysreview_analysis.R, and scripts/supplementary_analyses/compare_gpkg_gipt.R. All other analyses run from the cached outputs in data_output/. To re-run, download each file and save it in data_cache/ using the file and folder names below.

Format: file or folder name - source - date downloaded - description, processing and citation. Versions are those available at the download date. "Used in" lists the scripts that read each file.

CHELSA_bio1_1981-2010_V.2.1.tif - CHELSA - downloaded c. December 2024 - Global mean annual air temperature (BIO1), climatological normals 1981-2010, CHELSA version 2.1, 30 arc-second (~1 km) resolution, global GeoTIFF, unmodified. Stored values are scaled (temperature in degrees C = value x 0.1 - 273.15). Downloaded from https://chelsa-climate.org/. Cite as Karger, D.N., Conrad, O., Böhner, J., Kawohl, T., Kreft, H., Soria-Auza, R.W., Zimmermann, N.E., Linder, H.P. & Kessler, M. (2017) Climatologies at high resolution for the earth's land surface areas. Scientific Data, 4, 170122. https://doi.org/10.1038/sdata.2017.122, and Karger, D.N. et al. (2021) Climatologies at high resolution for the earth's land surface areas. EnviDat. https://doi.org/10.16904/envidat.228. Used in: spatial_dataprep.R (MAT at each facility), spatial_figures.R (Figure 5b).

CHELSA_bio12_1981-2010_V.2.1.tif - CHELSA - downloaded c. December 2024 - Global annual precipitation (BIO12, kg m-2 year-1, scaled by 0.1), climatological normals 1981-2010, CHELSA version 2.1, 30 arc-second resolution, global GeoTIFF, unmodified. Source and citation as for bio1 above. Used in: spatial_dataprep.R (MAP at each facility), spatial_figures.R (Figure 5c).

Ecoregions2017 - RESOLVE - downloaded c. November 2025 - Shapefile of the 846 terrestrial ecoregions of the world and the 14 biomes they belong to (Ecoregions2017.shp plus .dbf, .prj, .shx), unmodified, CC BY 4.0. Downloaded from https://ecoregions.appspot.com/. Cite as Dinerstein, E., Olson, D., Joshi, A., Vynne, C., Burgess, N.D., Wikramanayake, E., et al. (2017) An ecoregion-based approach to protecting half the terrestrial realm. BioScience, 67, 534-545. https://doi.org/10.1093/biosci/bix014. Used in: sysreview_analysis.R (biome of each study location and each GEM facility, Figure S1), supplementary_analyses/compare_gpkg_gipt.R.

Hansen_GFC_treecover2000_aus.tif - Hansen et al. / Global Forest Watch - downloaded March 2025 - Global Forest Change version 1.11 (2000-2023), "treecover2000" layer: percent canopy closure (0-100) of vegetation taller than 5 m in the year 2000, 1 arc-second (~30 m) resolution. Downloaded as the 20 10x10 degree tiles covering 10-50 degrees S, 110-160 degrees E and merged into a single GeoTIFF for Australia (no other changes to values). Downloaded from https://storage.googleapis.com/earthenginepartners-hansen/GFC-2023-v1.11/download.html. Cite as Hansen, M.C., Potapov, P.V., Moore, R., Hancher, M., Turubanova, S.A., Tyukavina, A., et al. (2013) High-resolution global maps of 21st-century forest cover change. Science, 342, 850-853. https://doi.org/10.1126/science.1244693. Used in: spatial_dataprep.R (mean tree cover in each facility footprint).

Hansen_GFC_lossyear_aus.tif - Hansen et al. / Global Forest Watch - downloaded March 2025 - Global Forest Change version 1.11, "lossyear" layer: year of gross tree cover loss (stand-replacement disturbance or change from forest to non-forest), coded 0 = no loss, 1-23 = loss in 2001-2023, ~30 m resolution. Tiles downloaded and merged for Australia as for treecover2000 above. Source and citation as above. Used in: spatial_dataprep.R (fraction of each facility footprint cleared since 2001).

NVIS_MVG_07_tif - Federal Dept of Climate Change, Energy, the Environment & Water, Gregory McIntyre, Ruby Stephens - 2025-01-20 - GeoTIFF file of Australian national vegetation mapping, National Vegetation Information System (NVIS) version 7.0, present-day extent, mapped as Major Vegetation Groups (MVGs) at 100 m resolution. Converted from original .gdb geo database raster downloaded from https://fed.dcceew.gov.au/datasets/5e70b5afc36a4c458a2cceb313eb3889/about by Gregory McIntyre using QGIS on Linux (all other versions of R/QGIS used GDAL version that was too old to open this file). Folder contains .tif raster tif, plus .clr guide to raster values (and colour settings for QGIS), plus .xml (created when opened in QGIS). MVG codes are matched to names using data_input/mvg_codes_names.csv. Used in: spatial_dataprep.R (present-day MVG at each facility and within footprints, Figure S2b).

NVIS_V7_0_AUST_RASTERS_PRE_ALL_GEOTIFF - Federal Dept of Climate Change, Energy, the Environment & Water - downloaded 2025-01-21 - National Vegetation Information System (NVIS) version 7.0, estimated pre-1750 extent of Australian vegetation, 100 m resolution GeoTIFFs in Australian Albers projection, unmodified. nvis7_0_aust_pre_mvg_alb.tif maps Major Vegetation Groups (MVGs; first band used); nvis7_0_aust_pre_mvs_alb.tif maps Major Vegetation Subgroups and is not used. The .clr files list raster values and names. Downloaded from https://www.dcceew.gov.au/environment/land/native-vegetation/national-vegetation-information-system. Cite as Department of Climate Change, Energy, the Environment and Water (2024) National Vegetation Information System (NVIS) Version 7.0. Australian Government, Canberra. Used in: spatial_dataprep.R (pre-1750 MVG at each facility and within footprints, Figure S2a).

RD-LANDCAPAUS-02 - Vanessa Adams and Jayden Engert - 27-Jul-2022 - Mapped Agricultural Land Capability Classification Data for Australia V.20, cite as Adams, V, Engert, J (2022) Data from: Mapped Agricultural Land Capability Classification Data for Australia V.20. https://dx.doi.org/10.25959/kjdc-k508. Only land_capability.tif is used (existing_capability and pastoral_capability are not). Land capability is calculated in spatial_dataprep.R and plotted in spatial_figures.R but not reported in the paper.

solar_all_2024q2_v1.gpkg and wind_all_2024q2_v1.gpkg - Global Renewables Watch team - 2026-06-25 - v1 dataset release from Robinson, C., Ortiz, A., Kim, A., Dodhia, R., Zolli, A., Nagaraju, S. K., Oakleaf, J., Kiesecker, J., & Ferres, J. M. L. (2025). Global Renewables Watch: A Temporal Dataset of Solar and Wind Energy Derived from Satellite Imagery (arXiv:2503.14860). arXiv. https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2503.14860 at https://github.com/microsoft/global-renewables-watch/releases/tag/v1.0. Global solar installation polygons and wind turbine points detected from satellite imagery up to 2024 Q2, unmodified. Used in: spatial_dataprep.R (footprints of Australian facilities), supplementary_analyses/compare_gpkg_gipt.R.
